      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Acute nocturnal and recurrent pain of the limb in children or \"growing pains\" constitute a poorly known pathological entity. Growing pains occur in 20% of children aged 2 to 12. The diagnosis is made after ruling out all organic pathology: inflammatory, infectious, post-infectious, traumatic, metabolic, tumoral, vascular, hematologic, orthopaedic and benign pathology of children. The treatment requires analgesics and soft massage."},
